</script>

# Textarea

Displays a multi-line text field. Styled with theme tokens like the shadcn textarea, fills the width of its container, and grows with its content.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Textarea } from "#lib/components/ui/textarea/index.js";
</script>

<Textarea placeholder="Type your message here." />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/textarea.json
```

## Binding

Use `bind:value` to read and write the value. Event handlers such as `oninput` and `onchange` also pass through to the element.

<Demo section="binding" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Textarea } from "#lib/components/ui/textarea/index.js";

	let message = $state("");
</script>

<Textarea placeholder="Type your message here." bind:value={message} />
<p>{message.length} characters</p>
```

## Auto height

The textarea uses `field-sizing: content`, so it starts at the minimum height for its size and grows as you type. Content sizing ignores `rows`, so set `min-height` through `class` or `style` to raise the starting height, and `max-height` to make it scroll after a point. Browsers without `field-sizing` keep a fixed height that you can drag to resize.

## With label

Link a `Label` to the textarea with `for` and a matching `id`, so clicking the label focuses the field.

<Demo section="label" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Textarea } from "#lib/components/ui/textarea/index.js";
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";
</script>

<Label for="message">Your message</Label>
<Textarea id="message" placeholder="Type your message here." />
```

## With button

Place a `Button` below the textarea to submit it in a form.

<Demo section="button" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<form>
	<Textarea placeholder="Type your message here." />
	<Button type="submit">Send message</Button>
</form>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and the padding, minimum height, text size, and corner radius follow the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Textarea size="xs" placeholder="Size xs" />
<Textarea size="sm" placeholder="Size sm" />
<Textarea size="md" placeholder="Size md" />
<Textarea size="lg" placeholder="Size lg" />
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Textarea rounded="sm" placeholder="Rounded sm" />
<Textarea rounded="3xl" placeholder="Rounded 3xl" />
```

## States

Set `disabled` to dim the textarea and block interaction. Set `aria-invalid="true"` to show the invalid ring, such as for a field that failed validation.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Textarea placeholder="Disabled" disabled />
<Textarea placeholder="Invalid" aria-invalid="true" />
```

## API

The `Textarea` props extend the native `textarea` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends Omit<CompProps<"textarea">, "value"> {
	/** Current value (bindable) */
	value?: CompProps<"textarea">["value"];
	/** Padding, minimum height, and text size on the shared scale */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall text, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round and safe */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** Classes merged onto the textarea */
	class?: CompProps<"textarea">["class"];
}
```
